// EXPECT: currently-rejected
// Violates: docs/SPEC.md section 5.1 (chained comparison).
//
// All six comparison operators sit at one precedence level and associate left,
// so `a < b < c` parses as `((a < b) < c)`. The parser accepts it. The type
// checker rejects it:
//   error: operator '<' cannot be applied to Bool and Int
//
// That is the right outcome by the right mechanism: the specification calls for
// chained comparison to be an error, and a type rule delivers it without the
// parser needing a special case.

pub fn chained(shared a: Int, shared b: Int, shared c: Int) -> Bool {
    return a < b < c
}
